.TH GETSOCKOPT 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
getsockopt \- read a socket option
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/socket.h>
.B int getsockopt(int descriptor, int level, int option, void* value, socklen_t* length);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads an option into writable value storage. The length pointer supplies
capacity and receives the size returned by Linux. The option determines the
buffer type.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero, or \-1 with errno set. Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR setsockopt (3crunch),
.BR getsockopt (2)
